<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Franco-Dutch War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1672">1672</a>–<a href="/years/1678">1678</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Dutch War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Franco-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> War was fought from 1672 to 1678 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and its allies and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a>, later supported by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a>'s invasion in 1672 nearly destroyed the Republic, which survived by flooding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-water-line">Holland Water Line</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaties-of-nijmegen">Treaties of Nijmegen</a> in 1678 left the Dutch territory intact, while France gained Franche-Comté and towns in the Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/franco-dutch-war.jpg" alt="Franco-Dutch War" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DavidDijkgraaf · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Franco-Dutch_War_Collave.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
